WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.598 --> 00:00:03.491
- [Narrator] Haruo Nakajima is arguably

00:00:03.491 --> 00:00:06.563
the most famous Japanese
actor of all time.

00:00:06.563 --> 00:00:08.941
But you've probably never seen his face.

00:00:08.941 --> 00:00:11.312
That's because Nakajima
was inside the body

00:00:11.312 --> 00:00:14.645
of a giant monster that destroyed Tokyo.

00:00:20.763 --> 00:00:23.513
(dramatic music)

00:00:24.432 --> 00:00:27.382
(Godzilla roaring)

00:00:27.382 --> 00:00:29.192
- [Narrator] Shortly after
the end of World War II,

00:00:29.192 --> 00:00:31.573
Haruo Nakajima went to
work for the movie studio

00:00:31.573 --> 00:00:34.005
Toho Pictures in Tokyo, Japan

00:00:34.005 --> 00:00:36.805
to pursue his dream of becoming an actor.

00:00:36.805 --> 00:00:39.405
He got his start as a
stuntman in Samurai films

00:00:39.405 --> 00:00:43.572
such as Seven Samurai, which
were all the rage at the time.

00:00:49.523 --> 00:00:51.735
- [Narrator] But it was on the
set of a World War II film,

00:00:51.735 --> 00:00:54.104
Eagle of the Pacific, where
Nakajima caught the eye

00:00:54.104 --> 00:00:56.604
of the director, Ishiro Honda.

00:01:19.850 --> 00:01:21.832
- [Narrator] Nakajima met with
Honda and the production team

00:01:21.832 --> 00:01:24.410
for this new, untitled monster movie,

00:01:24.410 --> 00:01:27.020
but no one really had any
direction for his role

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:30.770
as the monster, so he
started doing research.

00:01:43.582 --> 00:01:45.403
- [Narrator] On top of that,
creating the creature's suit

00:01:45.403 --> 00:01:49.320
was no easy task, especially
in post-war Japan.

00:02:16.531 --> 00:02:18.571
- [Narrator] After six
grueling months of shooting,

00:02:18.571 --> 00:02:23.091
the first Godzilla movie was
released in Japan in 1954.

00:02:23.091 --> 00:02:26.841
No one had any idea how
it would be received.

00:02:46.622 --> 00:02:48.992
- [Narrator] Godzilla wound
up becoming one of Japan's

00:02:48.992 --> 00:02:51.332
most ubiquitous cultural milestones,

00:02:51.332 --> 00:02:53.272
both for its achievements in filmmaking

00:02:53.272 --> 00:02:57.622
and its message of the
dangers of atomic weapons.

00:02:57.622 --> 00:02:59.022
And Nakajima?

00:02:59.022 --> 00:03:02.052
He put on the monster
suit for 11 more movies.

00:03:02.052 --> 00:03:06.135
And at 87 years old, it
is the pride of his life.

00:03:16.102 --> 00:03:19.019
(Godzilla roaring)

